  "description": "Construction of a single storey front, side, and rear wraparound extension",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The scale, siting, and design of the proposed development would result in a visually discordant and incongruous addition that is&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt; that is excessively large and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;harmful to the architectural integrity of the host dwelling. It would disrupt the established symmetry and rhythm of the terrace row, undermining the cohesive built form that characterises the surrounding streetscape. This harm is particularly pronounced given the location of the application site within the Becontree Estate, a designated area of historic and architectural significance. The proposal fails to respect the prevailing pattern of development and would detract from the visual amenity and heritage value of the area and thus contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024) Policy D4 and HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP2, SPP6, DMD1, DMD4 and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)"
